# agent-notepad — merge behaviour for files two machines write concurrently.
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A notepad is pushed from more than one machine: each box's Stop hook
# commits its own journal, so `sessions/index.json` collides on almost every repin. MEASURED
# repeatedly on 2026-09-04/05 — the publish helper correctly refuses to checkpoint through a
# `UU`, so the collision costs a manual resolution every time.
#
# ⛔ NOT `merge=union`. That is the obvious one-liner and it CORRUPTS THIS FILE. git's union
# driver is LINE-BASED and does not know it is looking at JSON, so it concatenates both sides
# and drops the comma between them:
#
#     [                                      -> Expecting ',' delimiter: line 4 column 3
#       {"sessionId": "shared"},
#       {"sessionId": "laptop"}
#       {"sessionId": "poland"}
#     ]
#
# Measured, not assumed. Removing a visible conflict that way would produce an invisible
# corruption in the one file this estate has already destroyed twice.
#
# So: a CUSTOM driver that parses JSON, unions by sessionId, keeps the later measurement, and
# REFUSES (leaving a normal conflict) on an unparseable side, a shrinking union, or duplicates.
#
# ⚠️ REGISTRATION IS PER-CLONE, AND FAIL-SAFE. This attribute only NAMES the driver. Each clone
# must also run:
#
#     git config merge.loom-session-index.driver \
#       'python3 ~/.claude/hooks/agent-notepad/lib/merge-session-index.py %O %A %B'
#
# On a clone where that has not run, git falls back to an ordinary conflict — exactly today's
# behaviour — never to corruption. That is why shipping the attribute ahead of the config is
# safe, and why a missing registration is a nuisance rather than a hazard.
sessions/index.json merge=loom-session-index

# ⚠️ NOTES.md is deliberately NOT given a driver. Two machines editing prose is not a union:
# keeping both sides verbatim is right for append-only records and wrong for a rewritten
# section, and no mechanical rule can tell those apart. It stays a human (or agent) decision.
